# Deny the whole build context by default, then re-admit only what a COPY instruction names.
# The verifier image copies the authoritative test tree, the target-revision test-support package,
# the hash-locked manifest, and the Reward Kit surface; nothing else in this directory may enter
# the build.
#
# Every file the scorer READS must appear below. In the conan bundle group_map.json and
# baseline_manifest.json were added as scorer inputs while this allowlist still denied them, so
# test_output.py would have raised at import inside the real image while host-side probes passed
# because they copied the files by hand. Adding a scorer input means adding a line here.
*
**/.*

!authoritative
!authoritative/**
!authoritative-dvc-testing
!authoritative-dvc-testing/**
!requirements.lock.txt
!reward.toml
!test.sh
!test_output.py
!sets.json
!group_map.json
!baseline_manifest.json

# judge.toml IS re-admitted, and the Dockerfile moves it out of /tests to /judged before the
# image is sealed. Reward Kit recurses into child directories (runner.py _collect_child_inputs),
# so a judged TOML anywhere under /tests would join the deterministic invocation's TaskGroup,
# where an auth failure escapes litellm.Timeout, no except guards the group, and out_path is
# never written: the test score would die with the judge. Held in its own root, test.sh scores
# it in a second, shell-guarded invocation that cannot take the first one down.
!judge.toml
# which is adjudicated at rollout time over the recorded final diff and verification output, not
# inside this container. Admitting it would also be fatal: Reward Kit globs every *.toml in its
# scan directory and turns any file carrying a [[criterion]] table into a live LLM judge, which
# raises on a missing key and writes no reward at all. The verifier grades offline, so the file
# stays in the bundle for the rollout harness and out of the image.
